file=Market Intelligence/trend/custom/emerging-trends/SKILL.md · h=name: emerging-trends\ntype: custom\nstatus: built from scratch\nassigned_agent: trend (Market Intelligence / Trend & Signal Detection)\nportable: true\ndate_added: 2026-07-29\ntier: 3\ndescription: "Bottom-up trend detection — funding rounds \· patent filings \· academic paper velocity \· developer-tooling signals \· search-volume shifts \· category discussion. Every trend tagged confidence + source-count."\ntriggers:\n- emerging trends\n- trend spotting\n- what's emerging in X\n- trend watch\n- trend brief\n · p:=Bottom-up trend detection — the signals that surface before they hit the mainstream. Confidence-tagged (early / gaining / mainstream) with source count.\n · st:/ Protocol=```\n1. SCAN     funding rounds \· patents \· papers \· dev-tooling \· search-volume \· discussion\n2. CLUSTER  co-occurrence → candidate trends\n3. CONFIDENCE score by source-count + independence\n4. RETURN   trends table + confidence + source list\n```\n · i:=Confidence: `early` (< 3 independent signals) \· `gaining` (3-10) \· `mainstream` (> 10 across multiple source types).\n\nSources: Crunchbase (funding) \· USPTO Assignee search (patents) \· arXiv / Semantic Scholar (papers) \· GitHub trending / Stack Overflow trends (dev) \· Google Trends (search) \· Reddit / HN discussion.\n · of:=Table: trend \· confidence \· earliest-signal-date \· source count \· source list.\n · pr:=- **Never forecast.** Descriptive: "these signals exist"; not "this will happen."\n- **Confidence tag mandatory.**\n- **Every trend cites ≥ 3 sources for `gaining`+**.\n- **Independence matters** — 3 blogs citing each other = 1 signal.\n · tb=\| Failure \| Response \| · tb=\|---\|---\| · tb=\| Signal source unreachable \| Note absent; do not extrapolate \| · tb=\| Confidence-flip (early → mainstream fast) \| Flag for operator review; may indicate hype cycle \| · b:=- `macro-signals` (this agent) — top-down macro; complement.\n- `scope/market-entry-analysis` — timing input.\n- `research/primary-research` — validate trend via primary research.\n- `meta` (AI & Agents) — AI-specific trends.\n- Shared OS: `verification-before-completion`.\n · tb=\| Skill \| Required \| Optional \| Source line \| · tb=\|---\|---\|---\|---\| · tb=\| emerging-trends \| Web fetch (multi-source) \· File read/write \| Crunchbase MCP \· Semantic Scholar MCP \· Google Trends MCP \| All steps \|